      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108975",
      ":question/problem": "If $X_{1}\u223cN(42, 4^{2})$ and $X_{2}\u223cN(31, 3^{2})$ are independent and $Y = X_{1} + X_{2}$, calculate $P(Y \\ge 80)$. Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\u03a6(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$ | $0.00$ | $0.01$ | $0.02$ | $0.03$ | $0.04$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1.2$ | $0.8849$ | $0.8869$ | $0.8888$ | $0.8907$ | $0.8925$ |\n| $1.3$ | $0.9032$ | $0.9049$ | $0.9066$ | $0.9082$ | $0.9099$ |\n| $1.4$ | $0.9192$ | $0.9207$ | $0.9222$ | $0.9236$ | $0.9251$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
